        "original_id": "ffc3fa88-b3dd-5f0c-bacf-cb5ecf974079",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Dear America, Run Away Home, A Picture of Freedom: The Diary of Clotee, a Slave Girl, Color Me Dark: The Diary of Nellie Lee Love, The Great Migration North, Look to the Hills: The Diary of Lozette Moreau, a French Slave Girl\n- People: Patricia McKissack\n- Events: Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: American history, slavery, immigration, racism, women's suffrage, war, western expansion\n\nFacts:\n- The Dear America series covers many American history topics, including the Pilgrims' journey to the New World, the Salem Witch Trials, the French and Indian War, the American Revolution, the American Civil War, World War I, World War II, western expansion, slavery, immigration, nineteenth-century prairie life, the California Gold Rush of 1849, the Great Depression, Native Americans' experiences, racism, coal mining, the Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire, women's suffrage, the sinking of the RMS Titanic, the Battle of the Alamo, and the Vietnam War.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire occurred in New York City on March 25, 1911.\n- The Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire was the deadliest industrial disaster in New York City history and one of the deadliest in United States history.\n- Run Away Home is a 1997 book by Patricia McKissack.\n- Patricia McKissack wrote the Dear America books A Picture of Freedom: The Diary of Clotee, a Slave Girl, Color Me Dark: The Diary of Nellie Lee Love, The Great Migration North, and Look to the Hills: The Diary of Lozette Moreau, a French Slave Girl.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
